// Auto-generated — do not edit manually.
export const html = "<h1 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h1>\n<p>This post closes the series of three posts devoted to detecting chessboard-based calibration targets. We started from fundamental features detection: X-junction based on ChESS, then we solved the problem of identifying the grid structure starting from sparse cloud of X-junction features. Finally, we are solving the problem of establishing the correspondence between the detected image features and local metric calibration target coordinates. This problem should be solved during sensor calibration or metrology tasks with calibrated devices.</p>\n<p>We do not imply that the whole calibration target is visible in the image. It means that we need local references. There are several solutions widely used in computer vision and robotics, among them boards with fiducial markers and ChArUco boards as on the image below (an example from the <a href=\"https://github.com/PStelldinger/PuzzleBoard/tree/main\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">authors GitHub</a>)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/content/images/03-puzzleboard/example0.png\"></p>\n<p>Both these targets are supported in my <a href=\"https://github.com/VitalyVorobyev/calib-targets-rs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">calib-targets-rs</a> library. But I think the PuzzleBoard solution is the most interesting and practical one, so we will discuss it here in more detail. It is also based on an interesting mathematical problem.</p>\n<h1 id=\"1-quick-start\">1. Quick start</h1>\n<p>Before spending some time explaining mathematical beauty of thee PuzzleBoard solution, I want to begin with explaining the main idea, showing the API of my implementation and performance.</p>\n<p>The idea for self-identification is to use every board edge as one bit of information: dark or bright circle:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/content/images/03-puzzleboard/puzzleboard.svg\"></p>\n<p>A fairly small area (a 4x4 grid patch) contains enough information to uniquely establish the grid coordinates. The position encoding circles has the same scale as board cell, it makes this board working in extreme low resulituion, when only a cell only spans a few pixels.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes vitesse-dark vitesse-light\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#dbd7caee;--shiki-light:#393a34;--shiki-dark-bg:#121212;--shiki-light-bg:#ffffff\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> add</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> calib-targets</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> image</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes vitesse-dark vitesse-light\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#dbd7caee;--shiki-light:#393a34;--shiki-dark-bg:#121212;--shiki-light-bg:#ffffff\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4D9375;--shiki-light:#1E754F\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> calib_targets</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#DBD7CAEE;--shiki-light:#393A34\">detect</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4D9375;--shiki-light:#1E754F\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> calib_targets</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">puzzleboard</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\">PuzzleBoardParams</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\"> PuzzleBoardSpec</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4D9375;--shiki-light:#1E754F\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> image</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\">ImageReader</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">let</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\"> img</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\"> ImageReader</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">open</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">path</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">?.</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">decode</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">()</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">?.</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">to_luma8</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">let</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\"> spec</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\"> PuzzleBoardSpec</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">master</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4C9A91;--shiki-light:#2F798A\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">.</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4C9A91;--shiki-light:#2F798A\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">?</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">let</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\"> params</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\"> PuzzleBoardParams</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">for_board</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">spec</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#4D9375;--shiki-light:#1E754F\">match</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> detect</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">detect_puzzleboard</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">&#x26;</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">img</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">,</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\"> &#x26;</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">params</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\">    Ok</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">found</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\"> =></span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> println!</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77;--shiki-light:#B5695977\">        \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\">detected </span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">{}</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> labelled corners</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77;--shiki-light:#B5695977\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">        found</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">.</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#DBD7CAEE;--shiki-light:#393A34\">corners</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\">.</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">len</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">    ),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#5DA994;--shiki-light:#2E8F82\">    Err</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#BD976A;--shiki-light:#B07D48\">err</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">)</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#CB7676;--shiki-light:#AB5959\"> =></span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\"> println!</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77;--shiki-light:#B5695977\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\">no board detected: </span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\">err</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">}</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77;--shiki-light:#B5695977\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#666666;--shiki-light:#999999\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>\n<p>Using this code on my MacBook Pro M4 for a 640x480 image took 3.5 ms with 0.7 ms for ChESS corner detection, 1.6 ms for grid reconstruction (as discused in <a href=\"\">the previous post</a>), and 1.3 ms for the PuzzleBoard localization:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/content/images/03-puzzleboard/author_like_oblique.png\"></p>\n<p>And similar python API:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes vitesse-dark vitesse-light\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#dbd7caee;--shiki-light:#393a34;--shiki-dark-bg:#121212;--shiki-light-bg:#ffffff\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#80A665;--shiki-light:#59873A\">uv</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> pip</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> install</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#C98A7D;--shiki-light:#B56959\"> calib-targets</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>\n<p>Now, when we know the main method idea an know how to use the software, let't dive into beautiful math stying behing this simplicity and computational efficiency.</p>\n<h1 id=\"2-the-puzzleboard-pattern\">2. The PuzzleBoard Pattern</h1>\n<p>The maximal size of the PuzzleBoard is 501x501 cells. There are very specific reasons for this size, and it is our goal by the end of this section to understand the origin of this size and to be able to reason about the uniqness of the pattern. But first things first, we begin from simple building blocks.</p>\n<h2 id=\"de-bruijn-sequence-and-de-bruijn-graph\">De Bruijn sequence and De Bruijn graph</h2>\n<p>The sequence</p>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mn>00010111</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">00010111</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">00010111</span></span></span></span></span>\n<p>is called a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Bruijn_sequence\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">De Bruijn sequence</a> of order 3 over the alphabet <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{0, 1\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span>. This is a <em>minimal</em> <em>cyclic</em> sequence that contains every possible combination of 3 bits exactly once.</p>\n<section class=\"vv-block vv-block--definition\" data-kind=\"definition\"><div class=\"vv-block__title\">Definition</div><div class=\"vv-block__label\">De Bruijn sequence</div><div class=\"vv-block__body\"><p>A de Bruijn sequence of order n over an alphabet of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03148em;\">k</span></span></span></span> symbols is a cyclic sequence in which every possible length-<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> string appears exactly once as a consecutive window. Its length is therefore <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03148em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p></div></section>\n<p>This formulation of the task doesn't make it obvious how to build such a sequence. The situation is changed dramatically after formulating the equivalent graph problem. Let's introduce the De Bruijn graph.</p>\n<section class=\"vv-block vv-block--definition\" data-kind=\"definition\"><div class=\"vv-block__title\">Definition</div><div class=\"vv-block__label\">De Bruijn graph</div><div class=\"vv-block__body\"><p>A De Bruijn graph of order <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> has all length-<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(n−1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> strings as its vertices, and all length-<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> strings as its directed edges. An edge goes from the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(n−1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-symbol prefix of a string to its <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(n−1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-symbol suffix.</p></div></section>\n<p>For our example the vertices are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>00</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">00</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">00</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">01</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">01</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span></span></span></span>, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">11</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">11</span></span></span></span>, and the De Bruijn graph reads:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/content/images/03-puzzleboard/debruijngraph.svg\"></p>\n<p>The task of building a De Bruijn sequence is reduced to finding an <em>Eulerian cycle</em> in this graph.</p>\n<section class=\"vv-block vv-block--definition\" data-kind=\"definition\"><div class=\"vv-block__title\">Definition</div><div class=\"vv-block__label\">Eulerian cycle</div><div class=\"vv-block__body\"><p>An Eulerian cycle is a cycle that uses every edge exactly once.</p></div></section>\n<p>This graph problem has a well-established efficient algorithmic solution. Graph theory also gives the answer to the question of the number of different binary de Bruijn sequences of order <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(n) = 2^{2^{n-1}-n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10903em;\">N</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0369em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0369em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>\n<p>For <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span> it gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N(3) = 2^{2^{2-1}-3} = 2^{2^{1}-3} = 2^{1} = 2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10903em;\">N</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9869em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9869em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9869em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9869em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>. The second sequence is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>00011101</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">00011101</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">00011101</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>First hint that bridges this concept with grid localization is this.</p>\n<section class=\"vv-block vv-block--note\" data-kind=\"note\"><div class=\"vv-block__title\">Note</div><div class=\"vv-block__body\"><p>Observing <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> consecutive symbols uniquely determines the position in the cyclic sequence.</p></div></section>";
